msgsnd() and msgrcv()
---------------------

Important points:

	1. Design a structure

		A message structure must be designed by the programmer.

		It must contain:

			mtype (message type)
			message data

	2. Key is required

		A key is required to create or access the message queue using msgget().

	3. In receive, 4th argument is important

		The 4th parameter (msgtyp) in msgrcv() is very important.

		Possible values:

			0
			+ve
			-ve

	4. Flag plays an important role

		Flags like IPC_NOWAIT, MSG_EXCEPT, MSG_NOERROR control behavior.
msgctl()
--------

	msgctl() is used to perform message queue control operations. 

		int msgctl(int msqid, int cmd, struct msqid_ds *buf);
		
		msgctl() performs the control operation specified by cmd
		The operation is performed on the System V message queue identified by msqid

	struct ipc_perm 

		This structure defines ownership and permissions 

			struct ipc_perm {
			    key_t  key;        // Key supplied to msgget()
			    uid_t  uid;        // UID of owner
			    gid_t  gid;        // GID of owner
			    uid_t  cuid;       // UID of creator
			    gid_t  cgid;       // GID of creator
			    unsigned short mode; // Permissions
			    unsigned short seq;  // Sequence number
			};
		
	struct msqid_ds

		struct msqid_ds {
		    
		    struct ipc_perm msg_perm; // Ownership & permissions

		    time_t msg_stime;  // Time of last msgsnd()
		    time_t msg_rtime;  // Time of last msgrcv()
		    time_t msg_ctime;  // Time of last change

		    unsigned long msg_cbytes; // Current bytes in queue
		    msgqnum_t msg_qnum;       // Current number of messages
		    msglen_t msg_qbytes;      // Maximum bytes allowed in queue

		    pid_t msg_lspid; // PID of last msgsnd()
		    pid_t msg_lrpid; // PID of last msgrcv()
		};

	

	msgctl(msqid, IPC_STAT, &buf);
		
		* Copies info from kernel data structure 
		* Stores it into the msqid_ds structure pointed to by buf 


	msgctl(msqid, IPC_SET, &buf);

		* Writes values from user space msqid_ds structure to kernel 
		* Used to update
			
			* msg_perm.uid
			* msg_perm.gid
			* msg_perm.mode 

		* Also updates

			* msg_ctime 

	msgctl(msqid, IPC_RMID, NULL);

		* Removes the message queue 
		* message queue is destroyed from kernel space 

	msgctl(msqid, IPC_INFO, &buf);

		* Returns system-wide message queue limits
		* Information is stored in structure pointed to by buf 

	Return values 

		On Success 

			IPC_STAT, IPC_SET, IPC_RMID return 0

		On error 

			returns -1

Advantages of Message Queue 

	1. Both processes need not be alive at the same time 
	2. Transmitter can send data to a particular receiver using a message type 

Disadvantages of Message Queue 

	1. Slowest IPC mechanism 

Solution to Disadvantage 
	
	To overcome this disadvantage, shared memory IPC mechanism is used














		








































































